cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or adapt the Build Contract, please cite it as below and link back to the repository."
title: "The Build Contract"
abstract: >-
  A seven-document system for long, multi-session AI builds — designed to be excellent at
  the first 90% (getting a project moving fast from a good conversation) and, harder, at
  the last 10% (staying honest, coherent, and on-taste across dozens of sessions, context
  resets, and the design pivots every real project eventually makes). Rules are tiered and
  amendable through a logged protocol rather than quiet erosion; the handoff document is
  maintained from day zero rather than written at the ragged end of a dying context; and a
  fresh session proves it read the documents before it is given the assignment.
authors:
  - family-names: "Reid"
    given-names: "Walter"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/walterreid/build-contract"
url: "https://github.com/walterreid/build-contract"
keywords:
  - ai-assisted-development
  - agentic-coding
  - session-handoff
  - context-management
  - llm-agents
  - agents-md
  - documentation-system
  - project-template
